  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nIssued 237 AM MDT SAT SEP 19 2026\nA weak, broad low moving south of the region on Tuesday will\nbring a 10-20% chance of showers and thunderstorms to South-\nCentral Idaho that evening. Overall synoptic flow over the\nregion doesn't change too much though, with zonal flow to the\nnorth shifting in and out but continuing a slight warming trend\nthrough the week. The track of the weak low seems fairly\nconfident amongst models, although it is cut off from the\nprimary flow so some change is expected in future model runs.\nThe zonal flow moves firmly overhead Thursday night ahead of an\namplified trough off the West Coast. Chances for precipitation\nremain <5% through Friday, before guidance consensus brings the\ntrough closer for more favorable moisture flux. Saturday\nprecipitation chances rise to around 10% across the area, with\ntemperatures cooling down beyond that.",
